# production-master-mcp — canonical agent policy

The single source of truth for how agents work in this repo is **`AGENTS.md`** at the
repo root. Read it before making any change.

Key points it enforces (see `AGENTS.md` for the full, authoritative text):

- This repo is the **standalone MCP server** for the Production Master hosted service —
  it terminates the Model Context Protocol (Streamable HTTP `POST /mcp` and stdio) and
  forwards tool calls upstream. **All investigation logic is server-side and never lives
  here.**
- Auth is **opaque bearer pass-through** — never log, store, or persist a forwarded token.
- **No LLM/provider SDK imports** and **no server-side investigation logic** — CI
  grep-enforces both (the ip-guard job).
- Tool schemas come from the shared `@production-master/mcp-tool-contract` package; never
  redefine them here.
- CI runs on GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-latest` only; no secrets in code/config.
- Conventional Commits, `feat/`|`fix/` branches, squash-merge, green CI before merge.

Do not fork policy into this file — edit `AGENTS.md` instead.
